    <div class="section-label">About</div>
    <h2>One consultant. One methodology. One problem solved.</h2>

    <p style="color: var(--gray); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.85; max-width: 640px;">
      I'm an independent consultant based in Mexico City, operating fully remote.
      Since 2011, I have built and operated huhuGERMAN — a production language-learning
      platform serving real university students every trimester, where a typed domain
      contract governs what the AI is and is not allowed to do based on each user's
      current learning state. In 2024, the platform's own architectural failure became
      the proof of method: a missing domain contract was causing the system to ask users
      to process feedback they had no context for — and the fix was architectural, not cosmetic.
      I work with Series A–C SaaS companies where trial-to-paid conversion is a known
      problem and the analytics have not yet explained why the architecture causes it.
    </p>
